    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into the July 11 slate with high expectations, anchored by the elite offensive potential of **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.11). **Jackson Merrill** earns top billing today; despite a neutral park environment, he faces Trey Yesavage, whose elevated xERA of 4.55 provides a prime opportunity for **Jackson Merrill** to capitalize on his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a left-handed arm in Noah Cameron; his role at the top of the order and the significant park boost at his venue keep his floor high. **Kyle Tucker** (69.61) and **Andy Pages** (66.83) round out our premier outfield options, both benefiting from favorable matchups against Brandon Pfaadt. **Andy Pages** specifically draws a 2% boost for base-stealing potential due to the slow delivery of the opposing battery, a crucial factor given our emphasis on stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Miguel Vargas** (51.82) on the bench. While **Miguel Vargas** displays an excellent xwOBA of .398, he fell just short of our efficiency threshold compared to the balanced production expected from **Drake Baldwin** (60.06) and **Josh Jung** (58.72). The optimizer favored the consistent volume associated with the top-third of the order assignments for our starters over the marginal gains projected for **Miguel Vargas**. We are also keeping a close eye on the bench to see if **Jorge Polanco** (44.24) sees action, though he is currently benched due to a significant 45% rain risk and a difficult matchup against Edouard Julien, which drags his efficiency well below our preferred levels. \n\nManagers should note that several slots are currently flagged as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled the output for **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** based on projected positions, any deviations in the official batting order could recalibrate these daily scores. **Dominic Smith** remains our lowest-confidence start at 41.63; while he occupies a roster spot, he remains on a short leash today due to a negative platoon split against Matthew Liberatore and a low-leverage spot in the batting order. We are proceeding with the current configuration, prioritizing high-order access and favorable pitching matchups to maximize our 5x5 output.",
